  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Covid Collective Social Research Platform - phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will build on two years of RED-funded rapid response social science research on the impact of COVID-19, helping to pull together data and analysis to guide FCDO Posts, governments and the international community in managing the recovery from the pandemic. The Covid Collective project has a distinct development objective, supporting urgent, mid and longer term knowledge creation, synthesis and translation around the impact of COVID-19 and the policy relevant evidence to inform future decision making for ODA eligible countries whist also utilising a global lens to draw future policy lessons and &#x2018;what works&#x2019; in response to global shocks and pandemics. The programme funds a large number of projects which focus on development contexts and looks at country-level dynamics across a variety of themes. For a full list of projects see https://www.covid-collective.net/</narrative>
  </description>
